WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.353
Phone Calls.

2
00:00:01.633 --> 00:00:06.134
Day 23 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Communication phase.

3
00:00:07.884 --> 00:00:08.908
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.188 --> 00:00:13.903
Phone calls are harder than face-to-face talk because you can't see the other person.

5
00:00:14.183 --> 00:00:18.577
Prepare 3 bullet points, speak slowly, and confirm everything at the end.

6
00:00:19.927 --> 00:00:20.781
Part 1.

7
00:00:21.061 --> 00:00:22.106
Before you call.

8
00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.316
Write your goal:

9
00:00:24.596 --> 00:00:26.537
Reschedule appointment to Friday.

10
00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:30.273
Have details ready: booking ID, account number, dates.

11
00:00:30.553 --> 00:00:32.900
Have pen and paper for reference numbers.

12
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.503
Find a quiet place.

13
00:00:35.853 --> 00:00:36.727
Part 2.

14
00:00:37.007 --> 00:00:38.053
Opening the call.

15
00:00:39.303 --> 00:00:40.241
You could say:

16
00:00:40.521 --> 00:00:42.164
Hi, this is Ashish Gupta.

17
00:00:42.444 --> 00:00:45.985
I'm calling about my booking, reference 4X7Q2.

18
00:00:46.265 --> 00:00:49.017
I'd like to change the date to Friday the 14th.

19
00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:51.263
Part 3.

20
00:00:51.543 --> 00:00:52.738
Useful phrases.

21
00:00:53.988 --> 00:00:55.332
Here is a quick table:

22
00:00:55.612 --> 00:00:56.999
Situation, and Say.

23
00:00:57.279 --> 00:00:58.132
Didn't hear:

24
00:00:58.412 --> 00:01:00.119
Sorry, the line's not clear.

25
00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:01.593
Could you repeat that?

26
00:01:01.873 --> 00:01:02.663
Spelling:

27
00:01:02.943 --> 00:01:06.975
Could you spell that for me? / That's G for Goa, U for Umbrella...

28
00:01:07.255 --> 00:01:08.087
Numbers:

29
00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:09.604
Let me read that back:

30
00:01:09.884 --> 00:01:11.655
9 to 8-4 to 5...

31
00:01:11.935 --> 00:01:12.916
Put on hold:

32
00:01:13.196 --> 00:01:14.284
Sure, I'll hold.

33
00:01:14.564 --> 00:01:15.652
Wrong department:

34
00:01:15.932 --> 00:01:18.193
Could you transfer me to the billing team, please?

35
00:01:18.473 --> 00:01:19.497
Getting nowhere:

36
00:01:19.777 --> 00:01:20.844
I understand.

37
00:01:21.124 --> 00:01:23.087
Could I speak to a supervisor, please?

38
00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:24.135
Ending:

39
00:01:24.415 --> 00:01:29.833
Just to confirm: the appointment is Friday at 3 pm, ref 4X7Q2.

40
00:01:30.113 --> 00:01:30.967
Thank you!

41
00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:33.234
Part 4.

42
00:01:33.514 --> 00:01:34.453
Work calls.

43
00:01:35.703 --> 00:01:36.492
Start:

44
00:01:36.772 --> 00:01:38.692
Hi Rahul, is now a good time?

45
00:01:38.972 --> 00:01:40.423
It'll take 5 minutes.

46
00:01:40.703 --> 00:01:41.897
Unexpected call:

47
00:01:42.177 --> 00:01:43.991
Can I call you back in 10 minutes?

48
00:01:44.271 --> 00:01:45.764
I'm just finishing something.

49
00:01:46.044 --> 00:01:46.748
End:

50
00:01:47.028 --> 00:01:50.505
Great, I'll send a quick email summarising what we agreed.

51
00:01:51.855 --> 00:01:52.815
Part 5.

52
00:01:53.095 --> 00:01:54.311
Leaving a voicemail.

53
00:01:55.561 --> 00:01:57.439
Here is a template you can copy.

54
00:01:57.719 --> 00:02:01.132
Hi, this is Ashish Gupta from XYZ Technologies.

55
00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:03.183
I'm calling about the invoice for.

56
00:02:03.463 --> 00:02:04.359
October.

57
00:02:04.639 --> 00:02:10.676
Please call me back on 98450 to 12345.

58
00:02:10.956 --> 00:02:16.545
Again, that's 98450 to 12345.

59
00:02:16.825 --> 00:02:17.593
Thanks!

60
00:02:20.443 --> 00:02:23.835
Name, then reason, then number (said twice, slowly), then thanks.

61
00:02:25.185 --> 00:02:26.124
Part 6.

62
00:02:26.404 --> 00:02:27.833
Practice conversations.

63
00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:30.662
Rescheduling an appointment.

64
00:02:30.942 --> 00:02:32.969
Here is how the conversation goes.

65
00:02:33.249 --> 00:02:35.275
Good morning, City Dental Clinic.

66
00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.433
Hi, this is Ashish Gupta.

67
00:02:37.713 --> 00:02:39.761
I have an appointment with Dr.

68
00:02:40.041 --> 00:02:42.217
Rao on Thursday at 4 pm.

69
00:02:42.497 --> 00:02:43.755
Yes, I see it.

70
00:02:44.035 --> 00:02:47.235
I'd like to move it to Saturday morning, if possible.

71
00:02:47.515 --> 00:02:50.673
We have 10:30 or 1one-on-one5 on Saturday.

72
00:02:52.023 --> 00:02:53.623
The conversation continues.

73
00:02:53.903 --> 00:02:55.609
10:30 is perfect.

74
00:02:55.889 --> 00:02:56.721
Done.

75
00:02:57.001 --> 00:02:59.135
Saturday at 10:30 with Dr.

76
00:02:59.415 --> 00:03:00.204
Rao.

77
00:03:00.484 --> 00:03:01.807
Just to confirm:

78
00:03:02.087 --> 00:03:04.348
Saturday the 15th, at 10:30?

79
00:03:04.628 --> 00:03:05.652
That's right.

80
00:03:05.932 --> 00:03:06.871
Thank you.

81
00:03:07.151 --> 00:03:08.495
Have a nice day!

82
00:03:09.845 --> 00:03:11.125
A bad line at work.

83
00:03:11.405 --> 00:03:13.431
Here is how the conversation goes.

84
00:03:13.711 --> 00:03:15.482
Hi Ashish, about the release...

85
00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.853
Sorry, Ravi, you're breaking up.

86
00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.647
Could you say that again?

87
00:03:19.927 --> 00:03:22.231
I said, can we move the release to Thursday?

88
00:03:22.511 --> 00:03:23.898
Got it, Thursday.

89
00:03:24.178 --> 00:03:25.287
Which time?

90
00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:27.018
After 6 pm.

91
00:03:28.368 --> 00:03:29.968
The conversation continues.

92
00:03:30.248 --> 00:03:32.104
Thursday after 6 pm.

93
00:03:32.384 --> 00:03:33.323
Okay.

94
00:03:33.603 --> 00:03:37.571
The line is still bad, so I'll send you a message to confirm.

95
00:03:37.851 --> 00:03:39.024
Perfect, thanks.

96
00:03:39.304 --> 00:03:40.499
Thanks, Ravi.

97
00:03:40.779 --> 00:03:41.781
Talk soon.

98
00:03:43.131 --> 00:03:44.667
That's the end of this lesson.

99
00:03:44.947 --> 00:03:49.598
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

100
00:03:49.878 --> 00:03:56.001
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

